  "releaseNotes": "Added:\n- VerifyAsync now accepts an optional CancellationToken and passes it through\n  the verification HTTP call, so callers can cancel an in-flight check.\n\nChanged:\n- Empty, missing, or whitespace-only tokens now resolve to a failed result\n  immediately, without calling Cloudflare.\n\nFixed:\n- The field-level error message is now attached to the form field's model-state\n  key, so it surfaces through asp-validation-for instead of only the validation\n  summary.",
